<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35242" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-mŏlestus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very troublesome</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">atque hi non sunt permolesti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 1, 18, 2</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">permŏlestē</span></b> , <i>with much trouble</i> or <i>difficulty</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">permoleste ferre aliquid,</span>”
				<i>to be much vexed at a thing</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 58, § 131</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 15, 17, 1</span></i>.</div>
